TPM = 2.2, GTEx nTPM = 52.5, consensus = 52.5). In ovary, NFKBIL1 leads (|log2| = 3.43382, HPA = 2.1, GTEx = 32.5, consensus = 32.5). In testis, NFKBIL1 also leads (|log2| = 3.49985, HPA = 0.6, GTEx = 17.1, consensus = 17.1). (evidence: a48 row 0: gene=HIF3A, consensus_colon=52.5, hpa_colon=2.2, gtex_colon=52.5, abs_log2_colon=4.0634 | a49 row 0: gene=NFKBIL1, consensus_ovary=32.5, hpa_ovary=2.1, gtex_ovary=32.5, abs_log2_ovary=3.43382 | a50 row 0: gene=NFKBIL1, consensus_testis=17.1, hpa_testis=0.6, gtex_testis=17.1, abs_log2_testis=3.49985)\n- The HPA consensus nTPM is not an independent third replication cohort. The consensus file is a deterministic aggregation of the HPA and GTEx measurements, so it carries no independent information beyond what the two sources already provide. In the top-10 discrepancy tables, the consensus value equals the GTEx value in the leading cases (HIF3A colon: consensus = 52.5 = GTEx; NFKBIL1 ovary: consensus = 32.5 = GTEx; NFKBIL1 testis: consensus = 17.1 = GTEx), confirming that the consensus is dominated by the GTEx measurement when HPA values are low. Using the consensus as a third replicate would therefore inflate apparent reproducibility without adding new biological information. (evidence: a48 row 0: consensus_colon=52.5, gtex_colon=52.5, hpa_colon=2.2 | a49 row 0: consensus_ovary=32.5, gtex_ovary=32.5, hpa_ovary=2.1 | a50 row 0: consensus_testis=17.1, gtex_testis=17.1, hpa_testis=0.6)\n\n**Limitations**\n\n- The consensus nTPM is a deterministic function of the HPA and GTEx values; it cannot serve as an independent replication and its agreement with either source is circular by construction.\n- The gene universe is restricted to the 1,485 TF Ensembl genes present in the HPA master table; TFs absent from HPA are excluded from all analyses.\n- Spearman correlation measures rank agreement only; the median |log2 ratio| captures typical magnitude of absolute discrepancy but does not characterise the full distribution.\n- Two of the 1,485 TF genes had no GTEx row in at least one tissue and were excluded from eligibility, reducing the eligible set to 1,483 per tissue.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- a1 data \"Transcription factor gene set\" (1485 rows) from deep_research_hpa\n- a2 data \"Consensus RNA nTPM in colon, ovary, testis\" (1485 rows) from investigator_hpa of a1\n- a3 data \"GTEx RNA nTPM in colon, ovary, testis\" (1485 rows) from investigator_hpa of a1\n- a4 data \"RNA tissue specificity categories\" (1485 rows) from investigator_hpa of a1\n- a5 data \"HPA RNA nTPM in colon, ovary, testis\" (1485 rows) from investigator_hpa of a1\n- a6 data \"HPA nTPM renamed\" (1485 rows) from select of a5\n- a7 data \"GTEx nTPM renamed\" (1485 rows) from select of a3\n- a8 data \"HPA + GTEx joined\" (1485 rows) from join of a6, a7\n- a9 data \"log2 ratio colon\" (1485 rows) from compute of a8\n- a10 data \"log2 ratio ovary\" (1485 rows) from compute of a9\n- a11 data \"log2 ratio testis\" (1485 rows) from compute of a10\n- a12 data \"|log2 ratio| colon\" (1485 rows) from compute of a11\n- a13 data \"|log2 ratio| ovary\" (1485 rows) from compute of a12\n- a14 data \"|log2 ratio| testis\" (1485 rows) from compute of a13\n- a15 data \"Colon eligible\" (1483 rows) from filter of a14\n- a16 data \"Ovary eligible\" (1483 rows) from filter of a14\n- a17 data \"Testis eligible\" (1483 rows) from filter of a14\n- a18 data \"Colon eligible count\" (1 rows) from aggregate of a15\n- a19 data \"Colon Spearman\" (1 rows) from correlate of a15\n- a20 data \"Colon median |log2 ratio|\" (1 rows) from aggregate of a15\n- a21 data \"Ovary eligible count\" (1 rows) from aggregate of a16\n- a22 data \"Ovary Spearman\" (1 rows) from correlate of a16\n- a23 data \"Ovary median |log2 ratio|\" (1 rows) from aggregate of a16\n- a24 data \"Testis eligible count\" (1 rows) from aggregate of a17\n- a25 data \"Testis Spearman\" (1 rows) from correlate of a17\n- a26 data \"Testis median |log2 ratio|\" (1 rows) from aggregate of a17\n- a27 da